<content><page number="6"><link href="https://redgirlrising.com" x="363.916730917502" y="916.7309175019275" width="261.372397841172" height="20.046260601387818"/><link href="http://team700.ca" x="457.2089437162684" y="948.3423284502699" width="127.98766383962989" height="21.588280647648418"/></page><page number="14"><link href="https://www.livingskiesbasketball.com" x="233.61603700848113" y="869.6993060909792" width="464.14803392444105" height="16.962220508866615"/></page><page number="16"><link href="https://www.livingskiesbasketball.com/mentorship" x="376.2528912875868" y="762.5289128758675" width="302.2359290670779" height="195.8365458750964"/></page><page number="17"><link href="https://www.canva.com/design/DAFu-hc0lmk/edit" x="13.878180416345389" y="572.0894371626831" width="293.75481881264454" height="376.25289128758675"/></page></content><outline><node pageNumber="1" title="BRIGHTSPOTS"><node pageNumber="1" title="A knowledge mobilization project. Shining a light on programs with, by and for Indigenous girls and young women."/></node><node pageNumber="2" title="About this Resource"><node pageNumber="2" title="Page 3 Pages 4-5 Pages 6-9 Pages 10-13 Pages 14-17"/><node pageNumber="2" title="Table of Contents"/></node><node pageNumber="3" title="About the RE.sport Project"><node pageNumber="3" title="Click the icon to visit the  Re.sport website"/></node><node pageNumber="4" title="Meet the Team"><node pageNumber="4" title="Leah Ferguson"><node pageNumber="4" title="PROFESSOR  UNIVERSITY OF SASKATCHEWAN"/></node><node pageNumber="4" title="Audrey Giles"><node pageNumber="4" title="FULL PROFESSOR  UNIVERSITY OF OTTAWA"/></node><node pageNumber="4" title="Tara - Leigh McHugh"><node pageNumber="4" title="PROFESSOR  UNIVERSITY OF CALGARY"/></node><node pageNumber="5" title="Meredith Wing"><node pageNumber="5" title="RESEARCH ASSISTANT"/></node><node pageNumber="5" title="Destiny Fiddler"><node pageNumber="5" title="RESEARCH ASSISTANT"/></node></node><node pageNumber="5" title="Contributing Organizations"/><node pageNumber="6" title="Red Girl Rising Movement Society"><node pageNumber="6" title="GET IN TOUCH"/></node><node pageNumber="7" title="ABOUT"><node pageNumber="7" title="Red Girl Rising Movement Society is an Indigenous-led organization grounded in the belief that movement is medicine. We create culturally grounded, trauma-informed movement programs that support healing, leadership, and wellbeing for Indigenous peoples and communities, while remaining inclusive and responsive to the broader community depending on the initiative."/><node pageNumber="7" title="LOCATION"><node pageNumber="7" title="VANCOUVER ISLAND, BRITISH COLUMBIA PROGRAMS DELIVERED ACROSS VANCOUVER ISLAND AND BEYOND"/></node><node pageNumber="7" title="PROGRAM SPOTLIGHTS"/><node pageNumber="7" title="Keep reading!"/></node><node pageNumber="8" title="PROGRAM SPOTLIGHTS"/><node pageNumber="8" title="TEAM 700"><node pageNumber="8" title="WHO IT SERVES"/><node pageNumber="8" title="PROGRAM DESCRIPTION"><node pageNumber="8" title="Contact ivy@redgirlrising.com for more information!"/></node></node><node pageNumber="9" title="WINA WELLNESS"><node pageNumber="9" title="Wina Wellness is a culturally grounded movement program created exclusively for Indigenous women and girls. Rooted in strength, connection, and care, the program uses movement, culture, and community to support healing, empowerment, and wellbeing in a safe and supportive environment."/><node pageNumber="9" title="WHO IT SERVES"><node pageNumber="9" title="Indigenous women and girls"/></node><node pageNumber="9" title="VALUES AND APPROACH"><node pageNumber="9" title="Our work is Indigenous-led, trauma-informed, and relationship-based, centring choice, cultural safety, and the belief that when people are supported holistically, they can thrive."/><node pageNumber="9" title="Contact ivy@redgirlrising.com for more information!"/></node></node><node pageNumber="10" title="Ayalik Fund"><node pageNumber="10" title="Our Mandate"/><node pageNumber="10" title="What We Do"><node pageNumber="10" title="The Ayalik Expeditions program provides opportunities for Inuit youth to participate in canoe trips and other challenging expeditions, led by experienced outdoor educators and mental health support workers."/><node pageNumber="10" title="Get in Touch! info@ayalikfund.ca"/><node pageNumber="10" title="Visit the Website!  www.AyalikFund.ca"/></node></node><node pageNumber="11" title="Values and Philosophy"/><node pageNumber="12" title="PROGRAM SPOTLIGHT"><node pageNumber="12" title="12-day canoe trip  for Inuit girls  on Great Slave Lake, NWT"/></node><node pageNumber="13" title="Get in Touch! info@ayalikfund.ca"/><node pageNumber="13" title="\u201cI found love and peace on this trip. On my solo night I learned that there are good days and bad days, and you just have to look up and be a prouder person than who you were yesterday.\u201d Erika Otokiak, age 16"/><node pageNumber="13" title="\u201cIt was a life changing trip. I learned that anything I put my mind to, I know I can do it. I never wanted to participate in anything until I went for this trip. I feel like a totally different person now. And I quit my addiction \u2013 I\u2019m very happy and I\u2019m totally not gonna start again!\u201d Andrea Owpaluk, age 15"/><node pageNumber="14" title="Facebook: Living Skies Indigenous Basketball League"><node pageNumber="15" title="The league provides a holistic approach to sport, supporting every athlete\u2019s physical, mental, spiritual, and cultural aspects."/></node><node pageNumber="15" title="Who Can Participate?"/><node pageNumber="16" title="Program Spotlight"><node pageNumber="16" title="Female Coaches Mentorship Program"><node pageNumber="16" title="The program is another way for Indigenous girls and women to..."/><node pageNumber="16" title="Click the image below to read more about the program!"/></node></node><node pageNumber="17" title="LSIBL centres Indigenous cultures and teachings throughout their work and programs. Click the photo below to open their drill library and see some examples!"/><node pageNumber="18" title="Additional Information"><node pageNumber="18" title="Looking to partner with the RE.sport team?"><node pageNumber="18" title="SEND AN EMAIL TO RESPORT.KPE@UTORONTO.CA"/><node pageNumber="18" title="projectresport.com"/></node></node><node pageNumber="19" title="BRIGHTSPOTS"/></outline><labels/></FlowPaper_Zine_UIConfiguration>